Nature of the modifications
---------------------------

Substantial changes were made relative to upstream:

  * Replaced the browser kernel. Profiles run adryfish/fingerprint-chromium,
    installed only from an audited manifest with a pinned SHA-256, instead of
    the upstream Wayfern kernel.
  * Removed the hosted-account surface. There is no sign-in, no subscription,
    no remote entitlement delivery, and no reachable path to any Donut Browser
    cloud service. Cloud-tier IPC commands are not registered.
  * Added a local fingerprint Persona model with a stable per-profile seed,
    a capability matrix, and consistency gating between the proxy exit location
    and the profile's timezone and locale.
  * Added a local fingerprint audit suite, including a ten-cold-start stability
    check against the real kernel.
  * Rebranded the product, including its name, icons and data directories.
    "Donut Browser" and its logo are marks of the upstream project and are not
    used by CocoBrowser.

Third-party components
----------------------

Dependencies retain their own licences; see the respective package manifests
(package.json, src-tauri/Cargo.toml) and lock files.

The browser kernel (adryfish/fingerprint-chromium, a Chromium derivative) is
downloaded at runtime rather than bundled, and is covered by its own licence.
Its integrity is verified against a pinned SHA-256 before installation.

The GeoIP database (GeoLite2-City) is downloaded at runtime and is subject to
MaxMind's licence terms.

